From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: No allocation per RTP packet

Each packet cost four allocations: its buffer and its shared Message (packetize), and in the NACK history a
make_shared list node and an unordered_map node, freed when the packet left the history. The packetizer now
reuses its packets: a ring from the oldest, which is taken again, buffer and all, once nothing else holds it
(the history let it go and it was sent). The NACK history is a fixed ring indexed by sequence number: the
packetizer numbers consecutively, so it holds the latest maxSize packets as before.
---
--- a/include/rtc/rtppacketizer.hpp
+++ b/include/rtc/rtppacketizer.hpp
@@ -64,6 +64,11 @@
 private:
 	// The fragments of the last lent frame: their buffers are reused for the next one.
 	std::vector<binary> mFragments;
+	// The packets this packetizer made, a ring from the oldest (mPacketsNext): the oldest is reused, buffer and
+	// all, once nothing else holds it (the NACK history let it go and it was sent); else a new packet joins.
+	std::vector<message_ptr> mPackets;
+	size_t mPacketsNext = 0;
+	message_ptr newPacket();
 	static const auto RtpHeaderSize = 12;
 	static const auto RtpExtHeaderCvoSize = 8;
 };
--- a/src/rtppacketizer.cpp
+++ b/src/rtppacketizer.cpp
